# ── Docker/Fly build-context trimming ──────────────────────────────
# The image reinstalls deps (`pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`) and recompiles
# from source, so none of the below need to be uploaded. node_modules (~573M)
# and .git (~30M) were the entire cost of the multi-hundred-MB build context.

# Dependencies — reinstalled inside the image
**/node_modules

# Git metadata
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Compiled output — recompiled inside the build stage
**/dist
**/dist-auto-eval
**/dist-coverage

# Root-level test-coverage output.
# NOTE: do NOT ignore services/api/coverage/ — its *.json data assets
# (intents.json, safety-framework.json) are read at runtime and reach the
# image via the wholesale `COPY services/api services/api`. Only its generated
# results/ output is excluded.
/coverage
services/api/coverage/results

# Local env / secrets — must never enter the build context
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# The web app is a separate Vercel deploy; the API image never copies it
apps/web

# Tooling / editor / OS cruft
**/.turbo
**/.cache
**/*.log
.DS_Store
scratchpad
